; a homogeneous transform encodes rotation + translation in one matrix
; in 2D: 3x3 matrix [[R, t], [0,0,1]] where R is 2x2 rotation, t is 2x1 translation
; in 3D: 4x4 matrix [[R, t], [0,0,0,1]]
; in nD: (n+1)x(n+1) matrix
; composition: T_world = T1 · T2 · ... · Tn  (chain of transforms)
; this IS the scene-graph composition — each bone applies its local transform
; the kinematic chain is the product of all joint transforms from base to tip

(mantra homogeneous-transform
  (karma geometry-varga)
  (swarupa matrix transform)
  (yukta rotation-matrix displacement aayaama)
  (pratipaksha homogeneous-transform))
